invariant: INV-16
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: reduce_once picks a - m or a with an if where it selected with a
  mask, so whether a Montgomery product needed its last subtraction
  decides which path runs. For rsa_vp1 that fact is public, and the file
  is written to hold a secret operand all the same. The values stay
  right, so the vectors and bin/rsa_equiv_test pass; the count of what
  the compiler emits sees it. The pinned clang emits one more conditional
  branch for rsa_mont64.c on both 64-bit specs, 24 against the 23 its
  ceiling records.

--- old
    sub_masked(o, a, m, k, mask_of_bit(at_or_above(a, top, m, k)));
--- new
    if (at_or_above(a, top, m, k) != 0) {
        sub_masked(o, a, m, k, UINT64_MAX);
    } else {
        memmove(o, a, k * sizeof(uint64_t));
    }
